      "intent_record": {
        "hunk_index": 2,
        "change_category": "bug_fix",
        "intent_summary": "Fixes redundant state checking by introducing a secured flag to track successful state transitions before executing offload logic.",
        "what": "Added braces around the RXRPC_CONN_SERVICE_CHALLENGING state transition block and introduced a 'secured' boolean flag that is set to true when the state changes from CHALLENGING to SERVICE. Changed the subsequent condition from checking conn->state == RXRPC_CONN_SERVICE to checking the secured flag.",
        "how": "The change ensures the offload call state flipping logic only executes when a state transition from CHALLENGING to SERVICE actually occurred, rather than redundantly re-checking the connection state. This prevents potential race conditions and makes the control flow more explicit about tracking whether the state change was performed."
